  "description": "KADPAK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C71 H85 Gd5 N12 O30,2(C1 H2 Cl2),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.646-3.924 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.53-115.54°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C75H98Cl4Gd5N12O32.",
